WEBVTT

00:02.520 --> 00:07.190
<i>I'll pry open any locked doors in my way</i>

00:07.190 --> 00:11.520
<i>Charging at full speed, straight ahead</i>

00:09.480 --> 00:14.910
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold
in Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

00:11.520 --> 00:13.330
<i>That's how I live</i>

00:23.000 --> 00:29.750
<i>I keep turning them over in my mind</i>

00:29.750 --> 00:32.720
<i>All the things I want to do</i>

00:32.720 --> 00:39.970
<i>Even if I'm told that's not 
what's expected of me</i>

00:39.970 --> 00:43.310
<i>I don't plan on giving them up</i>

00:43.310 --> 00:51.870
<i>Ah, dreams are meant to be big</i>

00:51.870 --> 00:56.840
<i>I'll head where the shining coin points me</i>

00:56.840 --> 01:01.870
<i>And nothing can stop me</i>

01:01.870 --> 01:07.000
<i>I won't back down, I'll face forward</i>

01:07.000 --> 01:12.250
<i>So I can fulfill my dream</i>

01:12.550 --> 01:17.180
<i>I'll pry open any locked doors in my way</i>

01:17.180 --> 01:21.560
<i>Wind at my back, giving it my all</i>

01:21.560 --> 01:23.300
<i>That's how I live</i>

01:30.920 --> 01:32.450
Please help me!

01:34.190 --> 01:35.880
Ah! I'm sorry.

01:35.880 --> 01:37.740
Is this the right place for consultations?

01:37.740 --> 01:38.810
Yes.

01:39.540 --> 01:41.870
<i>Oh! I haven't gotten 
a consultation job in a while!</i>

01:42.230 --> 01:45.000
<i>It was worth having that sign made!</i>

01:46.210 --> 01:49.210
Tales from Paradise Restaurant

01:49.650 --> 01:52.550
Er... My name is Alina.

01:53.150 --> 01:57.040
I learned of this place from 
the servants at House Reiner.

01:57.040 --> 01:59.900
Ah, those three...

01:59.900 --> 02:02.030
<i>I see. It was them, huh?</i>

02:02.560 --> 02:05.590
So what are you here to consult us about?

02:05.590 --> 02:06.930
Is something troubling you?

02:07.560 --> 02:09.610
Yes. In fact...

02:10.970 --> 02:14.230
My family runs a diner 
called Paradise Restaurant.

02:14.230 --> 02:16.900
In the kitchen is my father 
as the master chef,

02:16.900 --> 02:19.220
as well as one veteran and one apprentice.

02:19.220 --> 02:22.170
My mother and I work the floor.

02:23.930 --> 02:25.100
Mm-hmm...

02:25.450 --> 02:26.820
Mm-hmm...

02:28.730 --> 02:31.740
We're a small business with only five workers,

02:31.740 --> 02:35.770
but we're fortunate enough to get customers, 
so everything's been running smoothly.

02:35.770 --> 02:36.730
However,

02:37.300 --> 02:42.900
the second-born son to a large restaurant 
has begun to approach me incessantly.

02:45.340 --> 02:48.520
In other words, he's been 
trying to court you?

02:49.810 --> 02:50.910
Yes.

02:50.910 --> 02:54.490
But you see, I... have feelings for Anel...

02:54.490 --> 02:57.650
ah, the apprentice at our restaurant.

02:57.650 --> 02:59.750
Oh!

02:59.750 --> 03:02.230
Um... so that's why I...

03:02.970 --> 03:04.690
<i>I can't go out with you!</i>

03:04.690 --> 03:07.140
...said that and refused his advances.

03:07.140 --> 03:08.360
But then...

03:10.160 --> 03:13.610
Son of mine, just leave 
this to your old man.

03:13.610 --> 03:17.540
What if, oh, Paradise Restaurant 
were to run into trouble financially?

03:17.540 --> 03:21.880
There's no doubt that girl will come 
running into your arms for marriage.

03:22.300 --> 03:24.930
Then we can convert that dingy eatery

03:24.930 --> 03:28.410
into a new location for our 
restaurant, for you to take over!

03:28.410 --> 03:30.560
Not a bad idea, huh?

03:32.180 --> 03:33.560
Elder Sister Mitsuha!

03:33.560 --> 03:37.010
You see this takeover plot 
all the time in period dramas!

03:37.010 --> 03:38.470
I saw it in the dee vee d—

03:38.470 --> 03:42.130
Er, so, what exactly did they do?

03:42.130 --> 03:44.070
Did they pull a dirty trick?

03:46.650 --> 03:50.450
Our veteran worker suddenly quit.

03:51.330 --> 03:53.920
It seems he was poached by that restaurant!

03:56.160 --> 04:00.210
For a while, my father did his best 
to run the kitchen by himself,

04:00.900 --> 04:03.840
but then he ended up 
being attacked by ruffians!

04:07.710 --> 04:11.480
They made sure to specifically 
break only his dominant arm...

04:11.480 --> 04:12.600
How heartless!

04:12.600 --> 04:15.240
Obviously, he can't cook like this.

04:15.240 --> 04:16.860
So what about the restaurant?

04:17.520 --> 04:20.250
We've been closed for the past few days.

04:24.940 --> 04:26.360
I'm sorry...

04:27.130 --> 04:29.550
I'm begging you... please...

04:32.170 --> 04:35.350
"Always volunteer to wipe 
away a woman's tears."

04:35.350 --> 04:37.170
My brother's words.

04:38.960 --> 04:41.170
Let's begin by taking stock of the situation.

04:41.560 --> 04:43.880
The goals for now are 
to reopen the restaurant,

04:43.880 --> 04:48.210
continue operations, 
and prevent a financial downturn.

04:48.210 --> 04:51.610
In addition, to eliminate interference 
from the rival restaurant

04:51.610 --> 04:53.340
and prevent further meddling.

04:53.340 --> 04:57.070
And... if possible, tying the knot 
with that apprentice.

04:57.560 --> 04:59.130
Does that sound about right?

04:59.130 --> 05:00.480
Y-Yes...

05:00.930 --> 05:04.240
Understood. I'll take on this request!

05:04.880 --> 05:10.720
<i>General Store Mitsuha's consultation 
service has got its first case in ages!</i>

05:21.250 --> 05:22.090
Done!

05:22.090 --> 05:25.050
<b>Paradise Restaurant
Re-establishment Project</b>

05:25.780 --> 05:27.220
Let me introduce you.

05:27.220 --> 05:30.310
My father, Bernd. My mother, Stella.

05:30.310 --> 05:32.930
And... this is Anel, an apprentice.

05:32.930 --> 05:35.490
Nice to meet you. I'm Mitsuha.

05:35.490 --> 05:38.380
Getting right to the matter at hand here...

05:38.380 --> 05:41.860
For now, we should hire 
someone as soon as we can.

05:42.440 --> 05:47.410
Unfortunately, it'll be difficult to 
employ a new cook, as things stand.

05:47.410 --> 05:48.250
What?

05:48.820 --> 05:53.740
You're not likely to find skilled 
veteran chefs who are out of work.

05:54.130 --> 05:58.750
That being said, someone without experience 
won't be able to hit the ground running.

05:58.750 --> 06:03.340
If you're not careful, that large restaurant
might send in a chef of their own,

06:03.340 --> 06:05.260
and end up sabotaging you!

06:05.260 --> 06:07.130
So what do we do?!

06:07.130 --> 06:09.290
That's where this comes in!

06:08.930 --> 06:11.140
<b>Paradise Restaurant
Re-establishment Project</b>

06:09.290 --> 06:11.430
The Paradise Restaurant 
Re-establishment Project!

06:11.180 --> 06:19.350
<b>Reopen the restaurant with current staff,
instead of hiring unknowns, and resume operations</b>

06:11.430 --> 06:13.280
Item number 1, of 3!

06:13.280 --> 06:17.270
Reopen the restaurant with current 
staff, instead of hiring unknowns,

06:17.270 --> 06:19.350
and resume operations!

06:19.790 --> 06:22.870
That's not happening! Just look at my arm!

06:22.870 --> 06:25.070
Anel might be able to handle prep work,

06:25.070 --> 06:27.190
but he's still in training!

06:27.190 --> 06:29.600
He could never run the kitchen by himself!

06:30.060 --> 06:32.950
And Alina can only help out 
with simple tasks.

06:33.330 --> 06:35.830
Besides, if the three of us 
are in the kitchen,

06:35.830 --> 06:38.130
then Stella's the only one out on the floor.

06:38.130 --> 06:41.080
She can't wait on everyone and 
handle the bills by herself!

06:41.080 --> 06:43.680
I know what you're trying to say.

06:43.680 --> 06:46.070
I'm glad you listened to our problems.

06:46.600 --> 06:49.170
But there are things we can and can't do!

06:49.170 --> 06:54.050
Accomplishing that is the job of General 
Store Mitsuha's consultation service!

06:54.050 --> 06:55.150
What?!

06:57.500 --> 07:01.690
Master Bernd, why do you think it 
takes years for an apprentice chef

07:01.690 --> 07:03.920
to become fully fledged?

07:04.420 --> 07:06.720
That's because they get 
drilled in the basics,

07:06.720 --> 07:09.140
learn techniques from watching 
their master and more skilled chefs,

07:09.140 --> 07:10.490
practice during their free time...

07:10.490 --> 07:11.550
That's the thing!

07:12.070 --> 07:14.930
No one takes the time to 
teach apprentices anything,

07:14.930 --> 07:17.490
so they need to devote precious 
time from their busy schedules,

07:17.490 --> 07:21.210
and hone their skills little by little 
through trial and error!

07:21.210 --> 07:22.370
Isn't that right?

07:22.780 --> 07:23.910
Yeah...

07:23.910 --> 07:26.630
That's how all chefs end up 
becoming qualified.

07:26.630 --> 07:29.920
Then what if you were to 
watch over him all day long,

07:29.920 --> 07:33.390
teaching him the techniques and 
tricks needed to make a single dish?

07:34.300 --> 07:37.690
It doesn't need to be exactly 
the same as your cooking!

07:37.690 --> 07:40.710
Don't you think he could learn 
to get 90% of the way there?!

07:41.960 --> 07:45.310
The hardest part of cooking is that last 10%.

07:45.310 --> 07:49.430
If 90% is good enough, then even Anel 
might be able to do it as an apprentice.

07:51.650 --> 07:56.790
Then please hammer cooking knowledge into 
Anel and Alina's heads over the next week!

07:59.330 --> 08:01.330
<i>The master, constantly watching over me?</i>

08:01.330 --> 08:03.040
<i>Just me and Anel?!</i>

08:03.370 --> 08:05.630
But with just that,

08:05.630 --> 08:08.710
Stella will have to handle 
the floor alone, like I mentioned...

08:08.710 --> 08:11.850
Fear not, for I have a plan!

08:12.600 --> 08:16.770
Er... that, of course, includes the 
"tying the knot" part, as well, right?

08:18.820 --> 08:21.690
Rest assured! With my help, 
it'll be like sailing in a mud boat!

08:22.520 --> 08:25.060
That doesn't reassure me at all!

08:25.940 --> 08:28.900
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold in
Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

08:28.900 --> 08:31.940
<b>Saving 80,000 Gold in
Another World 
for My Retirement</b>

08:33.730 --> 08:35.160
<i>Yamano cuisine.</i>

08:35.890 --> 08:41.160
<i>A mysterious cuisine that suddenly 
became the talk of aristocratic rumors.</i>

08:42.310 --> 08:44.590
<i>The most exquisite of rare delicacies...</i>

08:44.590 --> 08:46.740
<i>The ultimate of sublimities...</i>

08:47.500 --> 08:51.730
<i>Countless chefs have tried 
to capture that fabled taste.</i>

08:51.730 --> 08:56.030
<i>However, it's said that none 
have managed to replicate it.</i>

08:57.330 --> 09:02.840
<i>Except one, who directly inherited those 
skills from the founder of Yamano cuisine.</i>

09:03.770 --> 09:06.340
According to that chef 
who became the first disciple,

09:06.340 --> 09:09.680
"Yamano cuisine is not 
the name of a single dish.

09:09.680 --> 09:14.120
All that is made using the 
Yamano skills is Yamano cuisine!"

09:14.550 --> 09:17.370
Huh... Sounds like some 
pretty amazing cuisine.

09:17.370 --> 09:19.280
It's <i>that</i> delicious?!

09:19.280 --> 09:21.270
I'd love to try it someday!

09:21.270 --> 09:23.830
Where do we have to go if we want some?

09:23.830 --> 09:25.680
Well, you'll never believe it!

09:27.080 --> 09:29.500
What?! Paradise Restaurant?

09:29.500 --> 09:32.040
Okay, one order of omelet rice!

09:32.040 --> 09:33.510
One order of udon!

09:34.520 --> 09:37.850
This is that famous Yamano cuisine, honey!

09:38.330 --> 09:40.930
Wow! Darling, it's amazing!

09:43.510 --> 09:44.980
One Hamburg steak up!

09:45.440 --> 09:47.070
Got it!

09:47.070 --> 09:49.170
<i>After a week of intensive training,</i>

09:49.170 --> 09:52.240
<i>Paradise Restaurant is open again as of today!</i>

09:54.190 --> 09:56.710
<i>Looks like the rumors have spread, as planned.</i>

09:56.710 --> 09:58.760
<i>Very good traffic for our first day!</i>

10:01.030 --> 10:05.330
And so, Paradise Restaurant 
Re-establishment Project, item 2 of 3!

10:05.970 --> 10:11.210
Implement measures to recoup losses from 
being closed, and generate a steady profit!

10:11.790 --> 10:15.080
And our course of action was, you 
guessed it, a word of mouth strategy!

10:15.080 --> 10:16.730
We asked a bunch of people for help,

10:16.730 --> 10:21.760
and had them spread rumors that you could 
eat Yamano cuisine at Paradise Restaurant.

10:22.590 --> 10:24.850
<i>But we don't want to go overboard here.</i>

10:24.850 --> 10:27.150
<i>It'd be bad if diners 
came flooding in, as well.</i>

10:27.150 --> 10:30.600
<i>What's important is having a long, 
steady stream of revenue.</i>

10:28.440 --> 10:32.400
<b>Implement measures to recoup losses from being closed,
and generate a steady profit</b>

10:30.900 --> 10:32.400
Mitsuha

10:32.400 --> 10:35.510
<i>And Yamano cuisine, 
just like the general store,</i>

10:35.510 --> 10:37.690
<i>is a lineup aimed at high 
margins and low volume!</i>

10:37.690 --> 10:42.050
<i>A slight luxury aimed at the wealthy, 
those looking to splurge on occasion,</i>

10:42.050 --> 10:45.390
<i>those who want to show off, and 
those celebrating an occasion!</i>

10:45.890 --> 10:48.580
<i>I've also prepared some 
inexpensive menu items, as well.</i>

10:48.580 --> 10:51.940
<i>Things you can make quickly and 
easily, with a low cost price!</i>

10:51.940 --> 10:53.040
<i>Like udon...</i>

10:53.770 --> 10:56.670
Grit, Ilse. Thanks for your hard work!

10:59.290 --> 11:02.180
<i>I submitted a designated request to 
have these two work as waitresses,</i>

11:02.180 --> 11:03.890
<i>on a seven-day contract.</i>

11:03.890 --> 11:06.000
How is it? Are you getting used to it?

11:06.000 --> 11:09.330
I'm sorry it's not a mercenary job this time.

11:09.330 --> 11:11.180
Ah, don't worry about it.

11:11.180 --> 11:12.700
All the hunting had burned us out,

11:12.700 --> 11:15.480
so we were thinking about 
taking a short break anyway.

11:15.480 --> 11:16.480
Besides...

11:16.480 --> 11:21.010
There's the designated request fee, 
wages from Paradise Restaurant,

11:21.010 --> 11:23.520
and even some tips from our guests!

11:23.520 --> 11:25.950
I'm happy to take on 
a mission like this any day!

11:25.950 --> 11:28.990
Not to mention all the delicious 
staff meals we can eat.

11:28.990 --> 11:30.160
It's the best.

11:30.160 --> 11:33.860
I'll be in the kitchen 
coaching them on Yamano cuisine,

11:33.860 --> 11:36.500
so let me know if you need anything from me.

11:36.500 --> 11:38.280
There's someone suspicious here...

11:43.030 --> 11:45.470
That's the owner of 
the restaurant we mentioned.

11:45.470 --> 11:46.890
I see...

11:46.890 --> 11:49.050
<i>Yamano cuisine, you say?</i>

11:49.050 --> 11:51.020
<i>Just what's going on here?!</i>

11:51.020 --> 11:53.950
<i>Despite all his schemes, business is booming.</i>

11:53.950 --> 11:56.360
<i>He must be real unhappy.</i>

11:56.670 --> 12:00.530
And that's where item 3 of 3 comes in!

12:00.650 --> 12:05.490
<b>Thwart the enemy's expectations,
and have him dig his own grave</b>

12:01.280 --> 12:05.120
Thwart the enemy's expectations, 
and have him dig his own grave!

12:05.850 --> 12:08.120
We've managed to have him panic,

12:08.120 --> 12:10.250
so let's leave him alone 
for now and keep watch.

12:10.250 --> 12:12.860
I'm sure he'll come meddling.

12:12.370 --> 12:21.470
<b>Inflict damage and fear to ensure 
he doesn't want to intervene ever again</b>

12:12.860 --> 12:17.060
Inflict damage and fear to ensure he 
doesn't want to intervene ever again...

12:17.060 --> 12:19.310
Hopefully we can accomplish up to this part.

12:20.010 --> 12:21.510
Mitsuha

12:21.470 --> 12:24.610
Well, that depends on what move he makes!

12:26.470 --> 12:28.700
What? You went to Paradise Restaurant?!

12:28.700 --> 12:29.810
I'm so jealous!

12:29.810 --> 12:31.890
Yamano cuisine was so good!

12:32.290 --> 12:34.640
<i>Day 5 since reopening for business!</i>

12:34.640 --> 12:36.960
I'll have one omelet rice, 
as well a bowl of udon.

12:36.960 --> 12:38.980
This is a Hamburg steak? Looks delicious!

12:38.980 --> 12:42.150
<i>They're dressed as commoners, 
probably to keep up appearances,</i>

12:42.150 --> 12:44.820
<i>but there are a handful of guests 
who look like they're nobles.</i>

12:44.820 --> 12:47.380
<i>If nobles and bigwigs end up 
becoming regulars here,</i>

12:47.380 --> 12:50.110
<i>it should stop your run-of-the-mill 
restaurant from meddling!</i>

12:50.110 --> 12:52.150
<i>We'll gain their favor!</i>

12:52.150 --> 12:53.580
<i>But...</i>

12:53.580 --> 12:56.080
<i>aren't we getting too many customers?</i>

12:56.490 --> 12:59.710
<i>Well, things are running 
smoothly in the kitchen!</i>

12:59.710 --> 13:02.000
<i>They've gotten to be pretty efficient!</i>

13:03.260 --> 13:05.160
It really has been troublesome.

13:05.840 --> 13:09.820
The products I ordered 
are taking ages to arrive.

13:09.820 --> 13:12.900
I heard there were monsters 
spotted around the border.

13:12.900 --> 13:14.230
Do you think that's the reason?

13:14.230 --> 13:15.680
<i>Monsters, huh?</i>

13:15.680 --> 13:18.830
<i>I forgot that those exist in this world.</i>

13:18.830 --> 13:22.360
<i>Monsters holding up distribution channels...</i>

13:22.360 --> 13:25.040
<i>And there was that gang that 
tried to kidnap Sabine...</i>

13:25.040 --> 13:26.620
<i>How dangerous.</i>

13:27.410 --> 13:29.660
Here's the omelet rice you ordered!

13:29.660 --> 13:32.370
<i>Yep. Sabine's been coming every day.</i>

13:32.370 --> 13:33.460
<i>To hang out...</i>

13:34.250 --> 13:35.660
<i>To help out!</i>

13:37.710 --> 13:41.290
<i>Well, the customers are happy, so it's fine.</i>

13:42.880 --> 13:44.220
<i>Hey, now.</i>

13:45.720 --> 13:48.440
<i>Exactly what is she jotting down in there?</i>

13:48.440 --> 13:50.640
<i>You're scaring your older sister...</i>

13:50.640 --> 13:52.980
But everything's looking hunky-dory!

13:52.980 --> 13:56.260
We can get back on track 
in a week, just like I planned...

13:56.730 --> 13:57.820
Out of the way!

14:01.890 --> 14:03.070
What's the matter?

14:03.070 --> 14:07.240
Looks like business is flourishing 
here at Paradise Restaurant.

14:08.360 --> 14:10.410
Just what do you want with us?

14:10.410 --> 14:13.580
I'm here today to perform my duty 
as an upstanding citizen,

14:13.580 --> 14:17.520
and bring charges of wrongdoing 
to Paradise Restaurant!

14:17.520 --> 14:18.960
Wrongdoing?

14:18.960 --> 14:20.460
Don't play dumb!

14:20.930 --> 14:24.100
I even have royal guards accompanying me!

14:24.100 --> 14:25.920
You can't talk your way out of this one!

14:25.920 --> 14:30.010
<i>He went so far as to bring guards with him, 
in order to launch a direct attack?</i>

14:30.010 --> 14:32.420
I'm afraid I don't know 
what you're referring to.

14:32.420 --> 14:35.040
If you could be so kind 
as to explain yourself.

14:35.040 --> 14:37.960
There! Indisputable proof!

14:38.780 --> 14:42.100
You're pretending to serve the Yamano 
cuisine that everyone's talking about,

14:42.100 --> 14:44.750
swindling customers out of money 
with your fraudulent act!

14:44.750 --> 14:46.990
Come now! You two guards!

14:46.990 --> 14:49.450
Arrest this man at once 
and throw him in jail!

14:49.940 --> 14:54.160
Um... do you have any proof that 
our Yamano cuisine isn't genuine?

14:55.160 --> 14:59.410
I figured you'd make an excuse like 
that, so I've brought him with me!

14:59.410 --> 15:01.620
The direct inheritor of Yamano cuisine!

15:01.620 --> 15:03.500
As the first disciple, he's a leading expert!

15:03.500 --> 15:08.050
Head chef of Viscount Reiner, 
Mister Marcel himself!

15:12.550 --> 15:14.720
Come, Marcel! Your testimony!

15:14.720 --> 15:19.280
No, I'm afraid I can't say anything 
without having a taste first.

15:19.280 --> 15:22.050
If I could have a sample of your offerings.

15:22.050 --> 15:23.610
M-Makes sense.

15:27.410 --> 15:32.740
Then I'll have some soup, this "omelet rice", 
as well as this "Hamburg steak".

15:33.700 --> 15:35.980
<i>Marcel hasn't heard of these dishes before!</i>

15:35.980 --> 15:38.240
<i>They surely must be phony!</i>

15:41.720 --> 15:43.290
Thank you for waiting.

16:05.700 --> 16:07.680
Who was the one who made these dishes?!

16:07.680 --> 16:11.490
<i>All right! Now this shop 
belongs to me and my son!</i>

16:11.490 --> 16:14.480
What's all the commotion? You're so loud.

16:14.480 --> 16:16.700
Just what is the meaning of this?!

16:16.700 --> 16:17.910
Yeah, that's right!

16:19.730 --> 16:21.080
How could you?!

16:21.080 --> 16:27.380
Why are you teaching this place how to 
make dishes I didn't learn about, Coach?!

16:27.380 --> 16:28.960
Yeah, that's right!

16:28.960 --> 16:31.790
Huh? What?!

16:31.790 --> 16:33.880
C-Coach?!

16:33.880 --> 16:35.250
S-S-So...

16:35.250 --> 16:38.180
The legendary founder 
of the fabled Yamano cuisine...

16:38.730 --> 16:40.930
i-is this little girl?!

16:43.780 --> 16:46.420
These are dishes to be 
served one portion at a time.

16:47.070 --> 16:49.980
Back then, we were serving 
food to feed a party.

16:49.980 --> 16:52.180
Of course I wouldn't teach you these.

16:52.180 --> 16:54.060
B-But, still!

16:54.060 --> 16:58.130
Serving dishes like these regularly 
for my lord and his family would be...

16:58.130 --> 17:01.180
Ah... then do you want to 
help in the kitchen?

17:01.180 --> 17:03.350
I'll teach you on the job.

17:03.350 --> 17:06.000
M-May I?! I'd love to!

17:06.380 --> 17:09.790
It'd be great if you could 
teach those two what you know.

17:09.790 --> 17:13.510
You could say that they're your 
fellow disciples, after all.

17:13.510 --> 17:14.710
Certainly!

17:18.780 --> 17:21.560
So... why are you here again?

17:24.280 --> 17:27.560
Is this the place where we 
can eat Mitsuha's cooking?

17:28.350 --> 17:29.560
Ah! Mitsuha!

17:30.310 --> 17:31.940
Beatrice!

17:31.940 --> 17:34.400
<i>Wait, that means...</i>

17:34.750 --> 17:35.950
Mitsuha.

17:35.950 --> 17:36.960
Mitsuha!

17:37.390 --> 17:38.340
Mitsuha!

17:38.340 --> 17:40.370
<i>The entire Bozes family is here!</i>

17:40.370 --> 17:41.910
A-Aristocrats?!

17:46.430 --> 17:48.970
Is this the establishment 
my daughter is working at?

17:50.240 --> 17:51.580
Ah, Your Majesty!

17:51.960 --> 17:53.530
Father!

18:01.180 --> 18:03.140
Y-Your Royal Majesty!

18:03.140 --> 18:04.920
Please allow us to escort you, as well.

18:05.470 --> 18:06.910
Hey, mister royal guard.

18:06.910 --> 18:11.040
Bernd was attacked some time ago, 
but I don't think they were ordinary ruffians.

18:11.040 --> 18:12.900
Do you think you could investigate?

18:17.490 --> 18:20.360
Royal guards, bring him to the station!

18:20.360 --> 18:22.210
Yes! Right away!

18:25.500 --> 18:29.430
<i>That should put at end to their 
interference with Paradise Restaurant.</i>

18:30.950 --> 18:32.520
A restaurant frequented by nobles,

18:32.520 --> 18:36.460
with the king himself dropping by 
and the princess serving as waitress?

18:36.460 --> 18:39.280
Where can you find a restaurant 
like that?! It doesn't exist!

18:39.280 --> 18:41.830
Huh? It's right here? I see...

18:42.170 --> 18:45.520
No, I couldn't have predicted 
this much! I swear it!

18:46.090 --> 18:49.000
It's overkill? Is that right?

18:50.170 --> 18:53.730
<i>I just hope that restaurant's owner 
doesn't receive capital punishment.</i>

18:54.630 --> 18:55.660
Mitsuha!

18:55.660 --> 18:58.760
I want to eat the food that you've made!

19:00.740 --> 19:02.140
I'd like to try it, as well!

19:02.140 --> 19:03.030
Me, too!

19:03.030 --> 19:05.820
I'm also done helping out for the day.

19:05.820 --> 19:08.610
Make me an omelet rice, Mitsuha!

19:08.610 --> 19:09.750
Sure thing.

19:10.410 --> 19:12.830
<i>I'll have the king pay me.</i>

19:15.820 --> 19:18.590
So, does this mean 
you've failed at your job?

19:18.590 --> 19:20.340
Huh? Wh-Why?!

19:20.340 --> 19:24.220
What happened to the 
"tying the knot" part?! Well?!

19:24.220 --> 19:26.350
Ah... slipped my mind.

19:27.090 --> 19:28.820
Excuse me, Your Majesty...

19:29.680 --> 19:32.900
Could I ask you for some matchmaking help?

19:33.380 --> 19:34.860
Don't you dare!

19:35.180 --> 19:36.760
Come now, Master Bernd.

19:36.760 --> 19:39.420
No need to be so distraught, just because you 
don't want your daughter to get married off.

19:39.420 --> 19:42.140
No! I don't mind taking him into our family!

19:42.140 --> 19:44.700
I'm not trying to stop you 
for a mundane reason like that!

19:45.360 --> 19:48.330
Huh? So what problem do you have, then?

19:48.810 --> 19:50.380
What's taking so long?

19:50.380 --> 19:51.820
I can't wait.

19:51.820 --> 19:53.080
I'm so hungry.

19:53.080 --> 19:54.630
I'm famished!

19:55.090 --> 19:58.020
Mitsuha, I'm hungry!

19:58.020 --> 19:59.960
Hurry it up!

20:07.920 --> 20:09.880
Good work out there, me.

20:17.590 --> 20:20.590
I didn't make that much 
money this time around.

20:21.160 --> 20:23.030
Well, I guess that makes sense.

20:23.030 --> 20:26.190
They reached out to me because 
their business was failing.

20:26.190 --> 20:30.340
<i>After deducting the pay for Grit and 
Ilse, as well as all the expenses,</i>

20:30.340 --> 20:32.080
<i>this was all that was left.</i>

20:32.710 --> 20:35.290
But I had fun, so it's fine!

20:35.290 --> 20:40.340
This gold coin's worth more than any money 
I could make by ripping off rich folks!

20:41.210 --> 20:43.050
<i>Along with money,</i>

20:44.680 --> 20:48.380
<i>I'm also gaining memories 
and allies in this world...</i>

21:01.920 --> 21:04.460
I wonder how Colette is doing...

21:14.830 --> 21:18.440
Colette, you've got a letter from Mitsuha.

21:18.440 --> 21:20.090
From Mitsuha?!

21:20.920 --> 21:21.890
Here.

21:27.390 --> 21:29.760
Mitsuha

21:27.830 --> 21:29.100
I'm doing a-okay!

21:30.130 --> 21:31.760
Mitsuha!

21:31.760 --> 21:33.580
Good for her.

21:34.060 --> 21:37.320
But the wagon sure did come late.

21:37.320 --> 21:38.380
Yeah...

21:38.380 --> 21:42.310
It seems it had to take the long way here, 
since it's been so dangerous lately.

22:05.840 --> 22:08.530
<i>I open my eyes, and where do I find myself?</i>

22:10.470 --> 22:13.180
<i>Maybe I should go back to bed</i>

22:15.060 --> 22:17.650
<i>Pretending I'm still half-asleep</i>

22:19.190 --> 22:23.710
<i>Running away from reality, 
to the west and east</i>

22:24.360 --> 22:26.120
<i>To be honest, life's all about</i>

22:26.120 --> 22:28.880
<i>Taking falls and getting back up 
(heavy damage)</i>

22:28.880 --> 22:31.990
<i>Hurt as it may, there's 
still a long road ahead...</i>

22:33.660 --> 22:36.450
<i>Looks like I've reached the end of my rope</i>

22:38.470 --> 22:40.960
<i>Hitting life's harder levels</i>

22:42.750 --> 22:47.320
<i>That's a test from the gods 
that I'll take on</i>

22:47.320 --> 22:49.780
<i>First things first, gotta be the economy!</i>

22:49.780 --> 22:52.430
<i>Aiming for the bourgeois life</i>

22:52.430 --> 22:54.180
<i>Gotta be the economy!</i>

22:54.180 --> 22:57.080
<i>No matter what enemies may come my way</i>

22:57.080 --> 22:59.140
<i>Gotta be the economy!</i>

22:59.140 --> 23:01.680
<i>I'll get them on my side</i>

23:01.680 --> 23:03.740
<i>Gotta be the economy!</i>

23:03.740 --> 23:06.280
<i>Who doesn't need money, after all?</i>

23:06.280 --> 23:10.990
<i>To the days where you need to 
scrape by one way or another</i>

23:10.990 --> 23:18.460
<i>Here's to you!</i>
